course: dictionary
lesson: 11394
title: Acceleration: getting faster
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Acceleration is the word for speeding up. When something gets faster and faster, it is accelerating. «The cyclist's acceleration down the hill made her smile.» The clue is down the hill: her speed was going up.
explain: In science, acceleration is how quickly speed changes. If speed goes up, that is acceleration. If speed goes down, that is a negative acceleration, which we call deceleration. «The car had good acceleration and reached 30 miles per hour in four seconds.»
explain: Acceleration is about change. A car moving steadily at the same speed is not accelerating, because its speed is not changing. Ask yourself: is the speed going up, going down, or staying the same?
fact: Acceleration means speeding up, or how quickly speed changes.
fact: An acceleration is one change in speed, and acceleration in general is uncountable.
fact: Slowing down is a negative acceleration, also called deceleration.
fact: Gravity makes falling objects accelerate, so they speed up as they fall.
fact: Acceleration can also mean any speeding up of a process, such as «the acceleration of climate change».
exercise: «The sprinter's acceleration at the start of the race was amazing.» What does acceleration mean here? | Slowing to a stop | A loud noise from the crowd | Staying in one place | *Speeding up quickly
exercise: Slowing down, when speed goes down, is a negative acceleration. What is another name for it? | Acceleration | *Deceleration | Stopping | Speeding
exercise: «A ball falls off the table.» What makes the ball accelerate? | Wind blowing it sideways | *Gravity pulling it down | Its colour | Its weight alone, with nothing pulling it
test: «The bus had poor acceleration on the hill, so it took ages to get going.» What does acceleration mean in this sentence? | The colour of the bus | How many seats it has | How loud its horn is | *How quickly the bus speeds up
test: Which of these is a negative acceleration? | Going at the same speed | Speeding up from rest | *Slowing down | Turning a corner
exam: Which sentence uses acceleration to mean any speeding up of a process? | The team won the game | The ball rolled slowly | The sun was hot | *The acceleration of climate change has sped up
